Content: whose a WebSocket without a frame is, for the embedder.

ContentBrowserClient::WillInterceptWebSocket() and CreateWebSocket() get a
null frame for a shared or service worker's socket and nothing else of it,
although WebSocketConnectorImpl knows the process that asked. An embedder with
a network policy per BrowserContext could not tell which applies: zebkit sent
every such socket to the one profile with a policy, and refused them all with
two. CurrentWebSocketInitiator() (content/public/browser/zebkit_websocket.h)
gives the process and the worker's DevTools token during those calls (and
GetWebSocketOptions()). A static set for the call's length rather than a new
field of WebSocketOptions, which content_browser_client.h, and so nearly all
of content, would be rebuilt for.

